pc|DQ|pc|S5|pc|SQ|pc|D5|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Over-ruffing is fine. When you have the master trump as a defender you should prefer to ruff if possible so as to draw a trump from declarer. On the other hand, an expert West would have counted out my hand. I have shown up with 3 clubs 3 hearts, 5 spades and 2 diamonds. So West would know he is entitled to only one more trick.|
PG| ***** 39 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Counting out declarer's hand as a defender is not that difficult. But you have to train yourself to do that. In my ^*BLesson Series on Basics of Defense^*n, on my website,  I discuss how to do that, and also how to count out declarer's high card points. You have all sorts of clues from the bidding and play. You just have to know how to use them. My lesson talks about how to do that.|
pg| ***** 40 ***** |


