%%%%%%Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/2an52ven
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   On November 27, 2024|pn|hondo717,Honeydog3,danpsych,marikaSz|
md|1SAQT963H4DT64CAK8,SK5HQT73DK9CJT742,SJ2HKJ8652DJ732CQ,S874HA9DAQ85C9653|sv|e|
mb|1S|mb|D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I don't agree with the double by West. The hand is a little light and has only two diamonds. It is okay these days to be a little light. But if you are light, then you should be short in the opponent's suit and/or have adequate support for the other 3 suits. I let it stand as I have a few teaching points on what would be the proper bid by North after the double.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


mb|2H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally, North could not bid 2@H because that is game forcing. However, once there is an intervening takeout double 2@H is actually a weak bid, showing less than 10 points. If North had 10+ points he would redouble. In fact, 3@H would not be out of the question as a preempt, although given the double, where West is somewhat likely to have hearts I think 2@H is best.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now normally East should consider bidding 3@D with 10 HCP but since I just let the double stand because I wanted to discuss the 2@H bid by North pass is fine.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


mb|2S|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 47 ***** |


