UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As I expected this worked out badly for me. But it shouldn't discourage you from preempting. There is some risk in preempting aggressively. But the rewards for preempting far outweigh the risks. Many players focus on the few bad results they get when a preempt doesn't work, while they forget about all the good results they get when it does work.|
PG| ***** 102 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^B@2^*BEast: ^*NCould I have opened my 15 points hand 1N with singleton spades instead of 1@C?|
PG| ***** 103 ***** |


cp|8|AT|
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|These days the ACBL allows you to open 1N with a singleton Ace, King, or Queen but not with a small singleton. I am not a big fan of doing that, although many players are.|
PG| ***** 104 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am a traditionalist when it comes to opening 1NT. One of the great strengths of opening 1NT is, because it is such a well defined bid, it leads to very accurate auctions. But once you start straying from the allowed distributions and HCP the auction accuracy goes down. Admittedly, my view is a minority view.

|
PG| ***** 105 ***** |


